<deck-scene id="s11" title="THE TEST" layout="split"><div>
<h2 class="rise">Fix the instant.<br><em class="serif">Name the zone.</em></h2>
<p class="lede rise">Data on both sides of the line.</p>
<button class="replay rise" data-replay="test"><deck-icon name="rotate-ccw"></deck-icon> REPLAY THE TEST</button></div>
<deck-compare class="rise" id="testCols">
<deck-col state="dim"><h3>THE BAD TEST</h3><p class="m">loadActivePublicPuzzle(new Date())</p><p>Passes or fails by where CI runs.</p></deck-col>
<deck-col><h3>THE REGRESSION</h3><p class="m">2026-05-21T00:30Z</p><p class="m">America/Los_Angeles</p><p>Assert the bound, not just the answer.</p></deck-col>
</deck-compare></deck-scene>

<deck-scene id="s12" title="SIX RULES" layout="full">
<h2 class="rise">Six rules, <em class="serif">one shape.</em></h2>
<deck-grid class="rise" id="ruleGrid" style="margin-top:28px">
<deck-cell><b>1 · Store a date key</b><span>Not a timestamp</span></deck-cell>
<deck-cell><b>2 · The zone makes the date</b><span>IANA, from the browser</span></deck-cell>
<deck-cell><b>3 · Cookie is input</b><span>Validate it</span></deck-cell>
<deck-cell><b>4 · UTC on purpose</b><span>Generation and inventory</span></deck-cell>
<deck-cell><b>5 · Bound the fallback</b><span>Never past the key</span></deck-cell>
<deck-cell><b>6 · Resolve once</b><span>Attempt uses the served date</span></deck-cell>
</deck-grid></deck-scene>

<deck-scene id="s13" title="CLOSE" layout="full">
<div class="finish rise">“Most recent.” “Today.”<br>Neither was enough.</div>
<p class="finish rise" style="margin-top:22px"><em class="serif">Whose today is it?</em><deck-mark inline></deck-mark></p>
</deck-scene>
